  "worked_solution": "We know that the denominator $|x|+{x}^{2}+1$ is positive for all values of $x.$ So, we can multiply both sides of the inequality by $|x|+{x}^{2}+1$ and solve the resulting inequality as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+7}{|x|+{x}^{2}+1} & \\ge \\frac{x+4}{|x|+{x}^{2}+1} \\\\ (|x|+{x}^{2}+1)\\cdot \\frac{2x+7}{|x|+{x}^{2}+1} & \\ge (|x|+{x}^{2}+1)\\cdot \\frac{x+4}{|x|+{x}^{2}+1} \\\\ 2x+7 & \\ge x+4 \\\\ x & \\ge -3 \\\\ x & \\ge \\,-3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
